WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.280
All right.

00:04.280 --> 00:05.400
So now I'm going to start with this.

00:05.400 --> 00:06.920
I'm going to show you an SQL code.

00:06.920 --> 00:11.760
And then quickly I'm going to explain for you the basic elements that you can find in each SQL code.

00:11.760 --> 00:13.360
So now we have this SQL code.

00:13.360 --> 00:17.080
And we call the whole thing an SQL statements query.

00:17.120 --> 00:19.560
And that's because it starts with a Select.

00:19.600 --> 00:22.360
And now the first thing that we see here is something green.

00:22.360 --> 00:23.920
This is the comments comment.

00:23.920 --> 00:25.440
It is just a note from you.

00:25.440 --> 00:28.080
And SQL will not execute this part of the code.

00:28.120 --> 00:31.040
And now what else we can see in our code is clauses.

00:31.040 --> 00:33.880
So our query is split into three main sections.

00:33.880 --> 00:35.840
And each section we call it clause.

00:35.840 --> 00:40.960
So here we have the Select clause, the From clause and the where they are like different sections that

00:40.960 --> 00:43.640
has specific tasks like for example the selects.

00:43.640 --> 00:48.800
It's all about to select the columns and the from clause focus on from which table we want to get the

00:48.800 --> 00:52.560
data, and the Where clause has the task of filtering the data.

00:52.600 --> 00:54.960
Now the next one we have the keywords.

00:54.960 --> 01:00.160
They are SQL standard reserved words that define a command or an operator.

01:00.160 --> 01:02.040
And as you can see, all of them are blue.

01:02.040 --> 01:07.520
So once you see something blue in SQL, that means it is a keyword and it has a specific operation.

01:07.520 --> 01:10.720
And you can see in this code all of them are uppercase, right?

01:10.720 --> 01:12.360
So all of them are capitalized.

01:12.360 --> 01:14.680
And this is the best practices how to write them.

01:14.680 --> 01:20.040
If you are writing an SQL code, make sure each time you have something blue make it completely capitalized

01:20.080 --> 01:20.800
uppercase.

01:20.800 --> 01:23.210
This makes it easier to read and to and understand.

01:23.210 --> 01:25.410
So make it, as a rule through the whole course.

01:25.450 --> 01:26.890
Now moving on to the next one.

01:26.890 --> 01:27.370
This one.

01:27.370 --> 01:30.650
The lower it is special keyword and we call it function.

01:30.650 --> 01:36.490
So they are like built in functions in SQL that accept an input, then process it and has at the end

01:36.490 --> 01:37.090
an output.

01:37.090 --> 01:41.530
So this function here takes the values from the country and makes it lowercase.

01:41.530 --> 01:44.250
So those functions can take something and transform it.

01:44.290 --> 01:46.330
Now what else we can see inside our query.

01:46.370 --> 01:50.850
We see those stuff name, country, customers country, those black words.

01:50.850 --> 01:52.450
We call them identifiers.

01:52.450 --> 01:54.970
They are just names of columns or tables.

01:54.970 --> 01:57.610
So for example the country here is a column name.

01:57.610 --> 01:58.170
Customers.

01:58.170 --> 01:59.610
Here is a table name.

01:59.610 --> 02:02.610
So they are just names for something in your database.

02:02.610 --> 02:04.090
So moving on to the next one.

02:04.090 --> 02:06.290
We have here something called operator.

02:06.290 --> 02:10.610
We usually use them inside the Where clause in order to compare two values.

02:10.610 --> 02:14.130
So it's simply going to go and compare the country with the value Italy.

02:14.130 --> 02:15.770
And we call those tough operators.

02:15.810 --> 02:18.450
Now the last one you can see here the red value.

02:18.490 --> 02:20.250
We call this a static value.

02:20.250 --> 02:23.290
It is something fixed that we have written inside our query.

02:23.290 --> 02:24.530
So my friends that's all.

02:24.570 --> 02:28.170
Those are the basic components of each SQL query.

02:28.170 --> 02:33.290
And you will find those elements not only in a Select statements but as well in the other stuff like

02:33.330 --> 02:35.050
the insert, create, delete.

02:35.050 --> 02:38.250
So they are the basic elements of any SQL code.

02:38.290 --> 02:38.570
Okay.

02:38.610 --> 02:41.570
So that's all about the basic components of the SQL code.

02:41.610 --> 02:45.010
Next we're going to deep dive into the Select statement in SQL.

02:45.050 --> 02:45.690
So let's go.
